{
  "id": 5,
  "title": "Food & drink",
  "goal": "Order food and drink, say what you want and don't want, talk about tastes and say what you like.",
  "intro": "Telugu food is famous across India for being **spicy**: Andhra chilli, tangy tamarind, pickles and *pappu* (dal) with rice and ghee. A Telugu meal centres on *అన్నం* (cooked rice) with a series of curries, *pappu*, *chāru* (rasam) and *perugu* (curd) to finish.\n\nGrammatically, wanting and liking are expressed with the **dative**: not 'I want coffee' but 'to me coffee is needed' (*నాకు కాఫీ కావాలి*).",
